    "body": "## Scope\n\nPublish I03.var05 version 1.0.0 as one bounded IN zero-delay child of the accepted I03.var01 `out_in` arm. The input changes only `ProblemDescription.PDESC` and the hour-10 IN `ResourceTransfer.TFDT` from 0.5 to 0. The OUT row, opening crew quantity two, seed, horizon, two aircraft and two mission waves remain fixed.\n\nThe original child log shows IN task start and arrival at hour 10, followed by a distinct local receipt. The ledger increments the local crew quantity once at receipt and closes at two. OUT departure remains hour 8. This accepts this fixed trace and report; it does not establish a general transfer timing law or outside-person identity.\n\n## Evidence and verification\n\n- One new serial SSH session-0 native run, `i03-var05-in-zero-delay-v100-ssh-20261008-01`; no accepted parent or prerequisite native run repeated. The runner held the existing global mutex throughout execution and checked actual GUI PID/session/start identity before and after each stage; root checked the live mutex and process guard before and after the dispatch. All six native/checker stages completed naturally with integer exit zero and empty stderr.\n- Converter gate before report export: zero errors, two declared warnings (#108 Control log and #126 teaching system without items), zero notes; calc step, original converter bytes and closure pin agree.\n- Independent sealed replay: 70,095 checks, all 5,210 report cells per arm, seven declared paired differences, 250 typed lines and 248 physical microsteps. Author trace has 184 timed events. The unchanged independent reader also passed after the actual catalog append with byte-identical verdict output.\n- Frozen 108 execution sources and 313-record prelaunch manifest remain unchanged. Final evidence index: 170,005 bytes, SHA-256 `c0ec9d87864a7adb88276d9410fa3567ff08f01c464824bd95b092c46e0fa486`; 233 source files, 140 mandatory accepted/new/native originals plus three separately mandatory zero-native preflight transport originals, and 80 accepted disk/Git source pairs.\n- Original binary streams, approvals, failed and superseded drafts, and old pins are retained. Local CRLF and Git LF catalog identities remain distinct. All new run/transport and publication source files are read-only; historical accepted raw byte seals are checked with their file attributes preserved.\n- Publication catalog appends entry 495; prior 494 entries and metadata remain type-exact unchanged, covering 107 distinct case IDs. Default planning consistency check and 14 related tests passed. This is separate from native acceptance; full local dictionary mapping still has the recorded M-B03 blocker.\n\nIndependent content, staged and exact remote-head review are required before the standing authorized merge. CI results will be reported from actual workflow/job evidence; no CI pass is inferred from local acceptance.\n\n## Boundaries\n\nOnly case artifacts and the publication index change on `simlox/main`; product `main` is unchanged. No general batch/priority/personnel identity, other transfer setup, GUI, performance or cross-engine claim. K01/K08 capture blockers remain without retries, and the I07 opening-stock-three diagnostic remains excluded. Issue #18 and the original overall Goal remain unfinished.\n\r\n",
    "title": "cases(simlox): I03 zero-delay IN transfer",
